# "The number of lands you control" is read as the ability resolves (CR 608.2c). Warped on turn 3 with two Islands and two Moxen, the
# Vestige is exiled at the end step and its leaves-the-battlefield ability goes on the stack with Bot1 controlling two lands. In response
# Bot2 sacrifices Strip Mine to destroy one of Bot1's Islands, so only one land is left: Mind Stone (mana value 2, which the count at
# trigger time would have allowed) is refused, and Sol Ring (1) is the control that is offered and put in tapped.

